.TH DATAPUMP-WORKER 1 "2026-09-28" "DataPump 001_00" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
datapump-worker \- socket-free Data Pump application worker
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B datapump-worker
.br
.B datapump-worker \-\-version
.br
.B datapump-worker \-\-self-check
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs the common C++ application using browser audio supplied by an embedding
host over inherited anonymous pipes. The host owns process lifetime, browser
transport, authentication and authorized file access. Data Pump opens no socket
and provides no HTTP server, URL, listening port or network fallback.
.PP
Standard input and output carry the versioned binary host protocol. Diagnostics
use standard error. Socket-backed descriptors and unqualified containment
platforms are rejected. Do not invoke the protocol interactively in a terminal.
.SH SECURITY
The embedding application must supply only the documented pipe endpoints and
approved file streams. Received data is never an executable command or a host
filesystem path. Receiving an attachment does not save or open it automatically.
The platform-specific no-socket boundary must pass qualification before use.
.SH FILES
.I share/datapump/web/hosted/
contains the declarative browser renderer and audio adapter for a host loader.
The renderer does not provide network transport.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR datapump-gui (1),
.BR pump (1)
